{"chunk_id": "0061bf594f2d", "text": "As King Sagara\u2019s sixty thousand sons dig through the earth searching for the stolen sacrificial horse, their violence throws the cosmos into turmoil. Devas, gandharvas, nagas, and other beings appeal to Brahma, who explains that the princes are doomed: the world is upheld by Vasudeva in the form of the sage Kapila, and the reckless princes will meet his wrath. Ignoring restraint, they tunnel across the world, encountering the colossal elephants that support the quarters of the earth. Finally they discover the horse peacefully grazing near the meditating Kapila. Mistaking the sage for the thief, they rush him with weapons and accusations. Kapila merely utters a powerful sound, and the princes are instantly reduced to ashes\u2014an example of divine power confronting arrogant force.\nSagara\u2019s sons dig through the earth seeking the stolen horse, accuse sage Kapila, and are instantly burned to ashes by his divine wrath.\nThemes: divine wrath, arrogance and punishment, cosmic order, quest for the sacrificial horse, encounter with Kapila", "vector": [0.012707059271633625, -0.01954828016459942, -0.007430514320731163, -0.024086516350507736, -0.02109263464808464, 0.014156585559248924, -0.03251273185014725, -0.01062759943306446, -0.022542161867022514, -0.015863504260778427, 0.006729458458721638, 0.0031835383269935846, 0.018721915781497955, 0.0024520019069314003, 0.014942309819161892, 0.0010668240720406175, 0.04251039773225784, -0.03023684211075306, 0.0199140477925539, -0.008934227749705315, 0.003381662769243121, -0.013689215295016766, -0.008690382353961468, 0.02214929834008217, -0.02709394320845604, 0.012300650589168072, 0.0103566600009799, -0.0094557860866189, 0.00013610473251901567, -0.02139066904783249, -0.016026068478822708, -0.018383240327239037, 0.002120101125910878, 0.004968352150171995, -0.016242818906903267, -0.008392348885536194, 0.007369552738964558, -0.010607278905808926, 0.0002944349544122815, 0.00019685443839989603